    "needsHostAccess" : false,
    "shortDescription" : "Runs hierarchical agglomerative clustering and generates a dendrogram image and summary report.",
    "longDescription" : "# agglomerative-clustering\n\nRuns hierarchical agglomerative clustering and generates a dendrogram image and summary report.\n\n## Input and outputs\n\nProvide a numeric CSV table as `features`. The implementation fits Ward/Euclidean\nagglomerative clustering on the first four columns. Supply feature columns without\nan identifier column.\n\n- `dendrogram_png`: a PNG file containing the SciPy dendrogram.\n- `report`: a plain-text summary of the fitted cluster count.\n- Metrics: `samples` and `clusters`, calculated from the fitted result.\n\n`distance_threshold` controls the clustering cut; its default `0.0` builds the full\nhierarchy. `plot_title`, `dendrogram_truncate_mode`, and `dendrogram_p` control the\nplot. The existing `linkage`, `metric`, `standardize`, `compute_distances`,\n`use_distance_threshold`, and `n_clusters` fields are retained for compatibility;\nthe current fitting implementation does not apply those settings.\n\n## Development\n\n```bash\npython3 -m venv .venv\nsource .venv/bin/activate\npip install -r requirements-dev.txt\ncp .env.example .env\n# Set APP_ID and platform URLs in .env before connecting.\npython main.py\n```\n\nThe Docker base image provides the FL-Net API. `requirements.txt` contains only\nadditional runtime dependencies; `requirements-dev.txt` includes the API for local development.\n\nBuild with `docker build -t tool-agglomerative-clustering .`.\nThe image runs as `nonroot` and uses Matplotlib's headless Agg backend.\n",
    "appConfig" : {
      "hyperparams" : [ {
        "default" : "ward",
        "description" : "Linkage strategy for hierarchical merges. Note: 'ward' requires metric='euclidean'.",
        "name" : "linkage",
        "options" : [ "ward", "complete", "average", "single" ],
        "type" : "CATEGORICAL",
        "variableName" : "linkage",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "1",
        "description" : "Store distances between merged clusters (needed for plotting an accurate dendrogram in some settings).",
        "name" : "compute_distances",
        "options" : [ ],
        "type" : "BOOLEAN",
        "variableName" : "compute_distances",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "1",
        "description" : "Standardize features to zero mean / unit variance before clustering (recommended).",
        "name" : "standardize",
        "options" : [ ],
        "type" : "BOOLEAN",
        "variableName" : "standardize",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "euclidean",
        "description" : "Distance metric for clustering (ignored when linkage='ward', which always uses euclidean).",
        "name" : "metric",
        "options" : [ "euclidean", "manhattan", "cosine" ],
        "type" : "CATEGORICAL",
        "variableName" : "metric",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "1",
        "description" : "If true, build the full tree with distance_threshold=0 and n_clusters=None to enable a dendrogram.",
        "name" : "use_distance_threshold",
        "options" : [ ],
        "type" : "BOOLEAN",
        "variableName" : "use_distance_threshold",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "2",
        "description" : "Number of clusters to cut the tree into (used only if use_distance_threshold=false).",
        "maxValue" : 200.0,
        "minValue" : 2.0,
        "name" : "n_clusters",
        "options" : [ ],
        "type" : "INTEGER",
        "variableName" : "n_clusters",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "Agglomerative Clustering Dendrogram",
        "description" : "Title text for the dendrogram.",
        "name" : "plot_title",
        "options" : [ ],
        "pattern" : "^.{0,120}$",
        "type" : "STRING",
        "variableName" : "plot_title",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "none",
        "description" : "Truncation mode for the dendrogram plot. 'none' shows the full tree; 'lastp' keeps the last P leaves; 'level' shows the last P merging levels.",
        "name" : "dendrogram_truncate_mode",
        "options" : [ "none", "lastp", "level" ],
        "type" : "CATEGORICAL",
        "variableName" : "dendrogram_truncate_mode",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "30",
        "description" : "Parameter P for truncate_mode 'lastp' or 'level' (ignored when truncate_mode='none').",
        "maxValue" : 10000.0,
        "minValue" : 1.0,
        "name" : "dendrogram_p",
        "options" : [ ],
        "type" : "INTEGER",
        "variableName" : "dendrogram_p",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      }, {
        "default" : "0.0",
        "description" : "Height at which to cut the dendrogram to form clusters (used only if use_distance_threshold=true). Set to 0.0 to compute the full tree like in the scikit-learn example.",
        "minValue" : 0.0,
        "name" : "distance_threshold",
        "options" : [ ],
        "type" : "FLOAT",
        "variableName" : "distance_threshold",
        "mode" : "BOTH"
      } ],
      "input" : [ {
        "description" : "Numeric feature table. The first four columns are used for clustering; provide features without an identifier column.",
        "mode" : "BOTH",
        "name" : "features",
        "required" : true,
        "type" : "CSV",
        "variableName" : "features"
      } ],
      "output" : [ {
        "description" : "PNG file containing the dendrogram plot.",
        "mode" : "BOTH",
        "name" : "dendrogram_png",
        "required" : false,
        "type" : "IMAGE",
        "variableName" : "dendrogram_png"
      }, {
        "description" : "Plain-text summary of the fitted cluster count.",
        "mode" : "BOTH",
        "name" : "report",
        "required" : false,
        "type" : "TEXT",
        "variableName" : "report"
      } ]
